<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RELEGATION ROUND RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RELEGATION ROUND RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPERE, Finland 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of relegation round matches at the ice hockey world championships on Tuesday:</p>
<p>Slovakia 2 Norway 1 (0-1 1-0 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Slovakia - Zdenko Ciger (34:06), Roman Kontsek (44:19)</p>
<p>Norway - Ole Dahlstrom (02:42)</p>
<p>Penalties: Slovakia 12 minutes, Norway 12</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,260 Latvia 8 Germany 0 (4-0 3-0 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Sergejs Zoltoks (00:56), Normunds Sejejs (01:47), Olegs Znaroks (16:18), Sergejs Cudinovs (19:58), Leonids Tambijevs (26:18, 56:23), Igors Pavlovs (29:58), Aleksandrs Kercs (36:54).</p>
<p>Penalties: Latvia 14 minutes, Germany 18</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,641</p>
<p>    Standings	  P   W  D  L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> 1. Latvia	     3   2  0  1  18   8    4</p>
<p> 2. Slovakia	   3   2  0  1   7   5    4</p>
<p> 3. Italy		2   1  1  0   7   6    3</p>
<p> 4. France	     2   1  0  1   5   6    2</p>
<p> 5. Germany	    3   1  0  2   2  10    2</p>
<p> 6. Norway	     3   0  1  2   6  10    1</p>
<p>Next matches: May 7 - Norway v France, Italy v Germany</p>
